1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:10,382
In this video you will learn how to run a voting poll with
NTSOne. Create a poll, build its ballot, open voting, and
watch the results arrive live.

2
00:00:10,982 --> 00:00:29,153
Open Voting Polls and choose New Poll. Give it a name and a
description. Then decide whether voters need an account. If
they do, they sign up and confirm their email. If not, anyone
with the link can vote straight away, and each browser counts
as one voter.

3
00:00:29,753 --> 00:00:42,576
Next, open the Ballot tab and add a position, such as
President. Add a candidate for each person on the ballot, with
an optional photo and short description. Then save the ballot.

4
00:00:43,176 --> 00:00:55,633
On the Overview tab you choose the rules. You can allow one
vote per email, show live results to voters, be emailed about
each vote, and decide whether voters must create an account.

5
00:00:56,233 --> 00:01:12,110
When everything is ready, press Open voting. You can also set
a time for the poll to close by itself. Voting can be free, or
you can ask voters to pay for their votes with the paid voting
settings, and agree to the platform fee first.

6
00:01:12,710 --> 00:01:26,332
This is what a voter sees. They open the link, choose one
candidate for each position, and press Vote. They are thanked
straight away, and if you allow it, the live results update as
people vote.

7
00:01:26,932 --> 00:01:38,155
When a poll asks for accounts, voters first sign in or create
an account. You can also limit voting to certain email
domains, or to a list of verified voters.

8
00:01:38,755 --> 00:01:51,732
The Results tab shows each candidate's votes, percentage and
place, and you can export them. The Voters tab shows who
voted, but never who they voted for, because the ballot stays
secret.

9
00:01:52,332 --> 00:02:01,390
That is how you run a voting poll with NTSOne. Use this video
as your guide, and watch the next video to learn about
businesses.
